WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.830
- [Male Narrator] An unparalleled design,

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.520
long-lasting battery performance,

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.500
and an innovative autonomous system.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.013
Introducing the Apple Car.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.830
- [Female Narrator] Well,
our version of the Apple Car

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.963
if a car could be made
out of iPhone parts.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.980
Apple's auto ambitions have
been rumored for years,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.860
and we still don't know if
they'll come to fruition.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.680
But what we do know is

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.610
that from self-driving capabilities

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.990
to running completely on battery power,

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.780
cars are becoming more and
more like giant gadgets.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.040
Even if you're not driving a
Tesla or new electric vehicle,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.230
there's a good chance
your car is still powered

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.930
at least in part by a computer.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.970
So what's next in the
digital car revolution?

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.210
- Today, traditional auto companies

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.660
need to radically change
how they do business.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.960
It's very different when you look at

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.400
how an electric and
autonomous car is built.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.610
It is more like a computer on wheels.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:58.620
- [Female Narrator] But what would it take

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.760
to make a car that's just as convenient

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.130
and well-integrated as an iPhone?

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.920
And what parts does Apple already

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.960
have experience engineering and producing?

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.040
To answer that, we had an idea:

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.230
crack open an iPhone and build a car

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.180
with the key automotive parts.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.400
Tom Forsyth, a 3D artists from London,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.130
was up to the challenge.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.700
We shipped him a bunch of
recycled iPhones and components,

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.030
he mocked up some ideas,

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.760
and we were cruising right along.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.968
- I would thoroughly not
recommend taking apart iPhones

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.290
unless you're a trained
professional for it

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.110
because you may get cut,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:35.430
you may set things on fire
in a very dramatic way.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.970
- [Female Narrator]
Okay, so not everything

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.830
in here is made of iPhone parts.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.470
The wheels, container for the seats,

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.470
and some other parts are 3D printed.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.400
But most of it is iPhone.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.290
And yes, this was made in London,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.080
so the steering wheel is on
the right side of the car.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.870
- [Tom] We tried to use as many

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.630
of the iPhone parts as possible.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.420
We used the entire back shell
and all of the main components

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.970
of the iPhone 11 to be the
kind of main undercarriage

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.990
and engine of the car, as it were.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.040
- [Female Narrator]
While Tom was building,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.570
we spoke to experts about the
technology that's going to be

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.860
core to the future of the car.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.630
Here's what we put together.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.870
One of the most important parts
of this computer on wheels:

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.190
the battery and the
infrastructure to charge it.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.950
Apple knows a thing about
batteries and chargers.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.930
Okay, fine. The Apple Car won't be charged

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:21.890
via lightning port,

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.000
and hopefully Apple doesn't
change the connector

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.430
every few years.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.560
But Apple has spent decades improving

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.240
its battery performance in everything

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.830
from phones to laptops to watches.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.570
But does that mean Apple could
just scale up its batteries

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:36.200
and put them in a car?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.880
We asked Jennifer Colgrove,
an automotive analyst

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.470
who spends a lot of time talking

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.680
with battery and car companies.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.000
- And each battery cell
still the fundamentally

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.370
same chemistry as the cell
you are using on your phone

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.260
or your laptop computer.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.720
They are the fundamentally
the same chemistry.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.640
But however when you pack
a lot of the batteries,

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.350
thousands of them, sometimes
even like tens of thousands

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:02.220
of cells together into a EV battery.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.010
So that is dramatic.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.150
- [Female Narrator] Most EV batteries

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:08.610
are made of some combination
of lithium ion and cobalt,

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.170
both high-demand materials
Apple's familiar working with.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.940
But to make car batteries

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.940
you'd need more land to build a factory,

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.590
more raw materials and
a labor force that knows

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.670
how to build EV batteries.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.330
Of course, Apple could
outsource its battery production

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.720
much like it does now
with its iPhone batteries.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.470
But Apple is known for
vertical integration,

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.450
controlling as much of the
supply chain as possible

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.750
like with its chips and processors,

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.800
another core, pun intended,

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.490
element to the computerization of the car.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.580
Apple has been making
its own A series chips

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:44.480
for the iPhone, iPad and Apple
watch for at least a decade.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.820
And in 2020, Apple announced plans

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.070
to end its 15 year partnership with Intel

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.780
to start making its
own very powerful chips

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.223
for its Mac computers.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.003
- [Male Narrator] And we call it M1.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.990
- [Female Narrator] These sorts
of chips can be used in cars

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.490
in a number of different ways,

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.460
but they're specifically very important

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.780
to autonomous driving,
explained Armando Periera.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.100
He brings together tech
and auto companies working

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.280
on self-driving cars.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.330
- When we talk about
computing, we're talking about

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.120
how can we squeeze all of these down

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.950
to a chip that is powerful enough

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.010
to run everything in parallel.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:26.700
So you can not steer now
and forget about the brakes

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.720
or engine control.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.200
You have to do all of these
things simultaneously.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.570
- [Female Narrator] Chips
that power everything

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.650
from collision warnings to touchscreens

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.430
and self-driving features
are in such high demand

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.830
that car makers have had
to suspend production

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.030
and furlough tens of thousands of workers

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.563
over recent shortages.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.680
Apple's new chip production sets itself up

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.830
as a major player amongst industry giants

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.460
like Intel, Qualcomm and Nvidia.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:54.060
- Of course, there's the chips
that do the data processing,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.540
but just having a chip
in the car isn't enough.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.060
There's actually a mass amount

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.210
of software that needs to be in place.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.470
- [Female Narrator] Danny
Shapiro leads marketing

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.400
for Nvidia's automotive business,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.670
which makes chips and
software to process data

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.470
for hundreds of car makers today,

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.580
including Mercedes-Benz, Toyota,

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.760
and Chinese EV makers
Nio, XPeng and Li Auto.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.640
- And so we've created a whole platform.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.020
It's called Drive.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.410
And that is the heart of the cars,

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.710
really the brain of the cars as well.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.580
So everything plugs into this brain.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.283
So you have cameras
that are looking forward

00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:30.700
or on the sides or in the back,

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.750
there's RADAR, there's LiDAR,

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.960
which is laser scanning.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.680
So all different senses.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.600
- [Female Narrator] Nvidia's
autonomous drive platform

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.270
is a decade in the making.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.600
And we don't know much about
Apple's autonomous ambitions,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.750
but CEO, Tim Cook, said they were working

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.830
on autonomous systems a few years ago.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.750
- We're focusing on autonomous systems.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.640
And clearly one purpose
of autonomous systems

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.440
is self-driving cars.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.040
There are others.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.300
- [Female Narrator] A
big part of autonomous

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.050
or self-driving technology
relies on cameras,

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.130
RADAR and other sensors to analyze

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.010
what's going on around the car.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.870
A lot of the self-driving
cars in development

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:11.390
today use LiDAR, or Light
Detection and Ranging technology.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.070
It's like RADAR, but instead
of using radio waves,

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:16.333
it measures distances using lasers.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.690
Apple has LiDAR scanners or cameras built

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.710
into its iPad Pro and iPhone 12 Pro,

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.490
enabling augmented reality features

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.970
like seeing how furniture would look

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.050
in your room before buying it.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.490
Put that technology on a car,

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.160
and you get a comprehensive
look at the roads around you.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.530
Building a car is in many
ways more complicated

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:36.950
than building an iPhone.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.600
So even if Apple has
the component knowledge,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.710
why would it even want to
enter the auto industry?

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.860
We asked Gene Munster,

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.240
an analyst that's been
covering Apple for years.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.820
- We spend a lot of time in cars,

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.550
and Apple wants to create products

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.860
that their mission is products
that enrich our lives,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.520
and a big part of our time
is spent moving around.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.010
- [Female Narrator]
Plus Apple has a history

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.570
of revolutionizing products.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:02.900
Remember Nokia phones or
BlackBerrys and iPods.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.143
- These are not three separate devices.

00:07:06.143 --> 00:07:06.980
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:11.980
This is one device, and
we are calling it iPhone.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.350
- [Female Narrator] And the Apple brand

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.260
is already part of the driving experience.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.640
CarPlay, which brings key Apple features

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.380
like maps, music and
messages to your dashboard,

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.513
has become a major selling point for cars.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:29.410
One survey found that 84%
of people aware of CarPlay

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.520
wanted to have the system
in their next vehicle.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.320
It wouldn't be too hard to imagine Apple

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.180
using a large iPad size screen

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:39.670
for the dash of a car that's
running its own software.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.930
And like the iPad and iPhone,

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:46.140
cars are now increasingly
dependent on software updates.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.010
If our experiment of turning an iPhone

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:49.740
into a car taught us anything,

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.160
it was that it certainly
be a massive undertaking

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.240
for the company.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.710
And despite having the cash in DNA for it,

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.170
that doesn't mean Apple will speed in

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:58.610
by building the whole car

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.370
or even releasing an Apple branded car.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.230
- A lesson I learned a long time ago,

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.470
which because Apple is
working on something,

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.570
doesn't mean it's gonna
see the light of day.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.030
I long prophesied that Apple

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.900
would come out with a TV and was wrong.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.650
- [Female Narrator] Apple
doesn't comment on rumors,

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:16.780
but we can say with 100% certainty,

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.650
if there's an Apple car it
will not look like this.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.840
And for now, this might be the closest

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.597
we get to an Apple Car.

00:08:23.597 --> 00:08:26.180
(gentle music)

